WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.200
All right, the news continues pouring in.
Things have simmer down a little bit from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:11.360
the inside insurrectionist riotous coup&nbsp;
attempt by Trump supporters that took place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.000
on Wednesday. But a lot of crazy is really going&nbsp;
on. I told you yesterday that Facebook and Twitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.480
had temporarily suspended Donald Trump for posting&nbsp;
election dissing for disinformation and incitement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.280
to violence. We have now heard from Mark&nbsp;
Zuckerberg. Facebook will be blocking Donald Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:31.120
on all its platforms, which includes Instagram,&nbsp;
at least until the end of his presidency. Mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:37.440
Zuckerberg made a post about this yesterday.&nbsp;
And, you know, I don't really care about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:43.760
Zuckerberg in the term in terms of evaluating his&nbsp;
morality and his personal politics. I know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:49.120
there's reason to be very upset as to how Facebook&nbsp;
has sort of looked the other way with a lot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.840
completely ridiculous ways that the Trump campaign&nbsp;
and the right have used Facebook to spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:01:00.080
disinformation and so on. This statement from Mark&nbsp;
Zuckerberg is what it is. And Zuckerberg wrote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:05.600
The shocking events over the last 24 hours clearly&nbsp;
demonstrate that President Donald Trump intends to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.640
use his remaining time in office to undermine&nbsp;
the peaceful and lawful transition of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:17.680
to his elected successor, Joe Biden. And he goes&nbsp;
on to say, We believe the risks of allowing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.480
president to continue to use our service&nbsp;
during this period are simply too great.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:27.200
Therefore, we are extending the block we have&nbsp;
placed on his Facebook and Instagram accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:32.960
indefinitely and for at least the next two&nbsp;
weeks until the peaceful transition of power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:40.080
is complete. So a an indefinite ban on Facebook&nbsp;
and Instagram for Donald Trump. And it's all just,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:47.440
you know, the struggle with these incidents is&nbsp;
that on the one hand, all of this stuff should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.240
have happened long ago. Trump's cabinet should&nbsp;
have considered the 25th Amendment long ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.880
Trump's cabinet should have resigned long ago.&nbsp;
Republicans should have abandoned Trump long ago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.600
Pence should have distanced from Trump long&nbsp;
ago on Twitter and Facebook, all this stuff.&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:10.000
But at this late stage, it's sort of like, come&nbsp;
on, guys, it almost feels like a virtue signal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.880
in some sense to me in order to really try to&nbsp;
rehabilitate one's image. And one could be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.720
person or a company when it's too little, too&nbsp;
late, when Trump is now already weakened and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:28.720
humiliated with just, you know, 12 days left until&nbsp;
the inauguration. So while these are obviously the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.880
correct decisions, it's hard to really feel&nbsp;
like, wow, it's so great. Everybody's now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:40.080
figuring it out. We figured it out before Trump&nbsp;
was even inaugurated and some of us were called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.560
alarmists. And, of course, every one of our worst&nbsp;
fears came true. So we'll continue to follow this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:53.200
I believe it's quite plausible Trump will&nbsp;
be permanently banned from Twitter as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:01.200
after he leaves office. But it is it's&nbsp;
really anyone's guess at this point. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.440
one of the things I think it's important&nbsp;
to remember, I mentioned this yesterday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:13.920
let's not allow the retroactive rehabilitation of&nbsp;
the image of a lot of these people that were along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:20.240
for the ride, ninety nine point nine percent&nbsp;
of Trump's term and now are bailing absolutely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:29.520
massive conflict within Trump's cabinet on&nbsp;
Wednesday as the violent insurrection was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.880
breaching the capital. Donald Trump denounced&nbsp;
Mike Pence and said Pence didn't do it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:40.800
Pence didn't do it. He didn't steal the election&nbsp;
for me. And that tweet was ultimately taken down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:44.480
by Twitter. And it was one of the tweets that&nbsp;
led to Donald Trump's suspension on Twitter.

